  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Suriname Development of Accounting &amp; Auditing Standards and Practices</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot; 1.  Strengthening the Capacity of the Suriname Institute of Chartered Accountants (SUVA) and developing the accountancy profession in Suriname. &quot;&quot;   Prepare a Strategic Plan for the Institutional Development of SUVA as a functional professional accountancy body having short, medium and long-term implementation plans. &quot;&quot;   Review the training needs of the local accountants and Accounting Technicians. &quot;&quot;   Design a Continuing Professional Development (CPD) program/curriculum for the accountants in Suriname, and implement a pilot run of key courses. &quot;&quot;   Develop a proposal for revised ethical standards, and disseminate the same, with the goal to finalize these during the life of the project. &quot;&quot;   Reviews the qualities of audit work carried out over a two year period, and disseminate the results. &quot;&quot;   Review the curriculum of University accountancy education and begin to introduce  IFRS in the curriculum 2.  Strengthening audit and oversight capacity of Rekenkamer Van Suriname - Supreme Audit Institution of Suriname (SAI). &quot;&quot;   Provide support preparing the annual public accounts. &quot;&quot;   Train the staff in conducting financial audits using international/INTOSAI auditing standards (ISSAIs). &quot;&quot;   Conduct a pilot financial audit of one financial year.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
